<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kushinagar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kusinara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kushinagar, ancient Kusinara, is a town in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, where according to Buddhist tradition the Buddha died and entered parinirvana. It was a centre of the Malla people, who cremated his body and shared out his relics. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lumbini">Lumbini</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bodh-gaya">Bodh Gaya</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarnath">Sarnath</a> it is one of the four main places of Buddhist pilgrimage, and its Mahaparinirvana Temple holds a large reclining Buddha.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kushinagar.jpg" alt="Kushinagar" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: myself · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kushinara1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
